---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDataRedactionSettings
---@field name? string Output only. Name of this Data Redaction Settings resource. Format: properties/{property_id}/dataStreams/{data_stream}/dataRedactionSettings Example: "properties/1000/dataStreams/2000/dataRedactionSettings"
---@field queryParameterRedactionEnabled? boolean Query Parameter redaction removes the key and value portions of a query parameter if it is in the configured set of query parameters. If enabled, URL query replacement logic will be run for the Stream. Any query parameters defined in query_parameter_keys will be redacted.
---@field emailRedactionEnabled? boolean If enabled, any event parameter or user property values that look like an email will be redacted.
---@field queryParameterKeys? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.StringList The query parameter keys to apply redaction logic to if present in the URL. Query parameter matching is case-insensitive. Must contain at least one element if query_parameter_replacement_enabled is true. Keys cannot contain commas.

---Settings values for data retention. This is a singleton resource.
---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDataRetentionSettings
---@field resetUserDataOnNewActivity? boolean If true, reset the retention period for the user identifier with every event from that user.
---@field eventDataRetention? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDataRetentionSettingsEventDataRetentionEnum Required. The length of time that event-level data is retained.
---@field name? string Identifier. Resource name for this DataRetentionSetting resource. Format: properties/{property}/dataRetentionSettings
---@field userDataRetention? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDataRetentionSettingsUserDataRetentionEnum Required. The length of time that user-level data is retained.

---@alias gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDataRetentionSettingsEventDataRetentionEnum "RETENTION_DURATION_UNSPECIFIED"|"TWO_MONTHS"|"FOURTEEN_MONTHS"|"TWENTY_SIX_MONTHS"|"THIRTY_EIGHT_MONTHS"|"FIFTY_MONTHS"

---@alias gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDataRetentionSettingsUserDataRetentionEnum "RETENTION_DURATION_UNSPECIFIED"|"TWO_MONTHS"|"FOURTEEN_MONTHS"|"TWENTY_SIX_MONTHS"|"THIRTY_EIGHT_MONTHS"|"FIFTY_MONTHS"

---A resource message representing data sharing settings of a Google Analytics account.
---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDataSharingSettings
---@field sharingWithOthersEnabled? boolean Enable features like predictions, modeled data, and benchmarking that can provide you with richer business insights when you contribute aggregated measurement data. The data you share (including information about the property from which it is shared) is aggregated and de-identified before being used to generate business insights. This field maps to the "Modeling contributions & business insights" field in the Google Analytics Admin UI.
---@field sharingWithGoogleAssignedSalesEnabled? boolean Allows Google access to your Google Analytics account data, including account usage and configuration data, product spending, and users associated with your Google Analytics account, so that Google can help you make the most of Google products, providing you with insights, offers, recommendations, and optimization tips across Google Analytics and other Google products for business. This field maps to the "Recommendations for your business" field in the Google Analytics Admin UI.
---@field sharingWithGoogleProductsEnabled? boolean Allows Google to use the data to improve other Google products or services. This fields maps to the "Google products & services" field in the Google Analytics Admin UI.
---@field name? string Identifier. Resource name. Format: accounts/{account}/dataSharingSettings Example: "accounts/1000/dataSharingSettings"
---@field sharingWithGoogleAnySalesEnabled? boolean Deprecated. This field is no longer used and always returns false.
---@field sharingWithGoogleSupportEnabled? boolean Allows Google technical support representatives access to your Google Analytics data and account when necessary to provide service and find solutions to technical issues. This field maps to the "Technical support" field in the Google Analytics Admin UI.

---A resource message representing a data stream.
---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDataStream
---@field iosAppStreamData? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDataStreamIosAppStreamData Data specific to iOS app streams. Must be populated if type is IOS_APP_DATA_STREAM.
---@field androidAppStreamData? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDataStreamAndroidAppStreamData Data specific to Android app streams. Must be populated if type is ANDROID_APP_DATA_STREAM.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Time when stream payload fields were last updated.
---@field displayName? string Human-readable display name for the Data Stream. Required for web data streams. The max allowed display name length is 255 UTF-16 code units.
---@field name? string Identifier. Resource name of this Data Stream. Format: properties/{property_id}/dataStreams/{stream_id} Example: "properties/1000/dataStreams/2000"
---@field webStreamData? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDataStreamWebStreamData Data specific to web streams. Must be populated if type is WEB_DATA_STREAM.
---@field type? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDataStreamTypeEnum Required. Immutable. The type of this DataStream resource.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Time when this stream was originally created.

---Data specific to Android app streams.
---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDataStreamAndroidAppStreamData
---@field firebaseAppId? string Output only. ID of the corresponding Android app in Firebase, if any. This ID can change if the Android app is deleted and recreated.
---@field packageName? string Immutable. The package name for the app being measured. Example: "com.example.myandroidapp"

---Data specific to iOS app streams.
---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDataStreamIosAppStreamData
---@field firebaseAppId? string Output only. ID of the corresponding iOS app in Firebase, if any. This ID can change if the iOS app is deleted and recreated.
---@field bundleId? string Required. Immutable. The Apple App Store Bundle ID for the app Example: "com.example.myiosapp"

---@alias gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDataStreamList gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDataStream[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDataStreamTypeEnum "DATA_STREAM_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"WEB_DATA_STREAM"|"ANDROID_APP_DATA_STREAM"|"IOS_APP_DATA_STREAM"

---Data specific to web streams.
---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDataStreamWebStreamData
---@field firebaseAppId? string Output only. ID of the corresponding web app in Firebase, if any. This ID can change if the web app is deleted and recreated.
---@field defaultUri? string Domain name of the web app being measured, or empty. Example: "http://www.google.com", "https://www.google.com"
---@field measurementId? string Output only. Analytics Measurement ID. Example: "G-1A2BCD345E"

---Request message for DeleteAccessBinding RPC.
---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDeleteAccessBindingRequest
---@field name? string Required. Formats: - accounts/{account}/accessBindings/{accessBinding} - properties/{property}/accessBindings/{accessBinding}

---@alias gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDeleteAccessBindingRequestList gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDeleteAccessBindingRequest[]

---A link between a Google Analytics property and a Display & Video 360 advertiser.
---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDisplayVideo360AdvertiserLink
---@field advertiserDisplayName? string Output only. The display name of the Display & Video 360 Advertiser.
---@field adsPersonalizationEnabled? boolean Enables personalized advertising features with this integration. If this field is not set on create/update, it will be defaulted to true.
---@field campaignDataSharingEnabled? boolean Immutable. Enables the import of campaign data from Display & Video 360 into the Google Analytics property. After link creation, this can only be updated from the Display & Video 360 product. If this field is not set on create, it will be defaulted to true.
---@field costDataSharingEnabled? boolean Immutable. Enables the import of cost data from Display & Video 360 into the Google Analytics property. This can only be enabled if `campaign_data_sharing_enabled` is true. After link creation, this can only be updated from the Display & Video 360 product. If this field is not set on create, it will be defaulted to true.
---@field advertiserId? string Immutable. The Display & Video 360 Advertiser's advertiser ID.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name for this DisplayVideo360AdvertiserLink resource. Format: properties/{propertyId}/displayVideo360AdvertiserLinks/{linkId} Note: linkId is not the Display & Video 360 Advertiser ID

---@alias gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDisplayVideo360AdvertiserLinkList gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDisplayVideo360AdvertiserLink[]

---A proposal for a link between a Google Analytics property and a Display & Video 360 advertiser. A proposal is converted to a DisplayVideo360AdvertiserLink once approved. Google Analytics admins approve inbound proposals while Display & Video 360 admins approve outbound proposals.
---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDisplayVideo360AdvertiserLinkProposal
---@field advertiserDisplayName? string Output only. The display name of the Display & Video Advertiser. Only populated for proposals that originated from Display & Video 360.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name for this DisplayVideo360AdvertiserLinkProposal resource. Format: properties/{propertyId}/displayVideo360AdvertiserLinkProposals/{proposalId} Note: proposalId is not the Display & Video 360 Advertiser ID
---@field validationEmail? string Input only. On a proposal being sent to Display & Video 360, this field must be set to the email address of an admin on the target advertiser. This is used to verify that the Google Analytics admin is aware of at least one admin on the Display & Video 360 Advertiser. This does not restrict approval of the proposal to a single user. Any admin on the Display & Video 360 Advertiser may approve the proposal.
---@field costDataSharingEnabled? boolean Immutable. Enables the import of cost data from Display & Video 360. This can only be enabled if campaign_data_sharing_enabled is enabled. If this field is not set on create, it will be defaulted to true.
---@field campaignDataSharingEnabled? boolean Immutable. Enables the import of campaign data from Display & Video 360. If this field is not set on create, it will be defaulted to true.
---@field advertiserId? string Immutable. The Display & Video 360 Advertiser's advertiser ID.
---@field adsPersonalizationEnabled? boolean Immutable. Enables personalized advertising features with this integration. If this field is not set on create, it will be defaulted to true.
---@field linkProposalStatusDetails? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaLinkProposalStatusDetails Output only. The status information for this link proposal.

---@alias gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDisplayVideo360AdvertiserLinkProposalList gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaDisplayVideo360AdvertiserLinkProposal[]

---Singleton resource under a web DataStream, configuring measurement of additional site interactions and content.
---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaEnhancedMeasurementSettings
---@field formInteractionsEnabled? boolean If enabled, capture a form interaction event each time a visitor interacts with a form on your website. False by default.
---@field fileDownloadsEnabled? boolean If enabled, capture a file download event each time a link is clicked with a common document, compressed file, application, video, or audio extension.
---@field streamEnabled? boolean Indicates whether Enhanced Measurement Settings will be used to automatically measure interactions and content on this web stream. Changing this value does not affect the settings themselves, but determines whether they are respected.
---@field scrollsEnabled? boolean If enabled, capture scroll events each time a visitor gets to the bottom of a page.
---@field searchQueryParameter? string Required. URL query parameters to interpret as site search parameters. Max length is 1024 characters. Must not be empty.
---@field uriQueryParameter? string Additional URL query parameters. Max length is 1024 characters.
---@field videoEngagementEnabled? boolean If enabled, capture video play, progress, and complete events as visitors view embedded videos on your site.
---@field siteSearchEnabled? boolean If enabled, capture a view search results event each time a visitor performs a search on your site (based on a query parameter).
---@field outboundClicksEnabled? boolean If enabled, capture an outbound click event each time a visitor clicks a link that leads them away from your domain.
---@field name? string Output only. Resource name of the Enhanced Measurement Settings. Format: properties/{property_id}/dataStreams/{data_stream}/enhancedMeasurementSettings Example: "properties/1000/dataStreams/2000/enhancedMeasurementSettings"
---@field pageChangesEnabled? boolean If enabled, capture a page view event each time the website changes the browser history state.

---An Event Create Rule defines conditions that will trigger the creation of an entirely new event based upon matched criteria of a source event. Additional mutations of the parameters from the source event can be defined. Unlike Event Edit rules, Event Creation Rules have no defined order. They will all be run independently. Event Edit and Event Create rules can't be used to modify an event created from an Event Create rule.
---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaEventCreateRule
---@field destinationEvent? string Required. The name of the new event to be created. This value must: * be less than 40 characters * consist only of letters, digits or _ (underscores) * start with a letter
---@field eventConditions? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaMatchingConditionList Required. Must have at least one condition, and can have up to 10 max. Conditions on the source event must match for this rule to be applied.
---@field parameterMutations? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaParameterMutationList Parameter mutations define parameter behavior on the new event, and are applied in order. A maximum of 20 mutations can be applied.
---@field sourceCopyParameters? boolean If true, the source parameters are copied to the new event. If false, or unset, all non-internal parameters are not copied from the source event. Parameter mutations are applied after the parameters have been copied.
---@field name? string Output only. Resource name for this EventCreateRule resource. Format: properties/{property}/dataStreams/{data_stream}/eventCreateRules/{event_create_rule}

---@alias gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaEventCreateRuleList gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaEventCreateRule[]

---An Event Edit Rule defines conditions that will trigger the creation of an entirely new event based upon matched criteria of a source event. Additional mutations of the parameters from the source event can be defined. Unlike Event Create rules, Event Edit Rules are applied in their defined order. Event Edit rules can't be used to modify an event created from an Event Create rule.
---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaEventEditRule
---@field processingOrder? string Output only. The order for which this rule will be processed. Rules with an order value lower than this will be processed before this rule, rules with an order value higher than this will be processed after this rule. New event edit rules will be assigned an order value at the end of the order. This value does not apply to event create rules.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of this event edit rule. Maximum of 255 characters.
---@field parameterMutations? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaParameterMutationList Required. Parameter mutations define parameter behavior on the new event, and are applied in order. A maximum of 20 mutations can be applied.
---@field name? string Identifier. Resource name for this EventEditRule resource. Format: properties/{property}/dataStreams/{data_stream}/eventEditRules/{event_edit_rule}
---@field eventConditions? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaMatchingConditionList Required. Conditions on the source event must match for this rule to be applied. Must have at least one condition, and can have up to 10 max.

---@alias gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaEventEditRuleList gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaEventEditRule[]

---Event setting conditions to match an event.
---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaEventMapping
---@field minEventCount? string At least one of the following four min/max values must be set. The values set will be ANDed together to qualify an event. The minimum number of times the event occurred. If not set, minimum event count won't be checked.
---@field maxEventCount? string The maximum number of times the event occurred. If not set, maximum event count won't be checked.
---@field eventName? string Required. Name of the Google Analytics event. It must always be set. The max allowed display name length is 40 UTF-16 code units.
---@field minEventValue? number The minimum revenue generated due to the event. Revenue currency will be defined at the property level. If not set, minimum event value won't be checked.
---@field maxEventValue? number The maximum revenue generated due to the event. Revenue currency will be defined at the property level. If not set, maximum event value won't be checked.

---@alias gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaEventMappingList gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaEventMapping[]

---A resource message representing an `ExpandedDataSet`.
---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaExpandedDataSet
---@field dimensionFilterExpression? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaExpandedDataSetFilterExpression Immutable. A logical expression of ExpandedDataSet filters applied to dimension included in the ExpandedDataSet. This filter is used to reduce the number of rows and thus the chance of encountering `other` row.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the ExpandedDataSet. Max 200 chars.
---@field metricNames? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.StringList Immutable. The list of metrics included in the ExpandedDataSet. See the [API Metrics](https://developers.google.com/analytics/devguides/reporting/data/v1/api-schema#metrics) for the list of dimension names.
---@field description? string Optional. The description of the ExpandedDataSet. Max 50 chars.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name for this ExpandedDataSet resource. Format: properties/{property_id}/expandedDataSets/{expanded_data_set}
---@field dataCollectionStartTime? string Output only. Time when expanded data set began (or will begin) collecing data.
---@field dimensionNames? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.StringList Immutable. The list of dimensions included in the ExpandedDataSet. See the [API Dimensions](https://developers.google.com/analytics/devguides/reporting/data/v1/api-schema#dimensions) for the list of dimension names.

---A specific filter for a single dimension
---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaExpandedDataSetFilter
---@field fieldName? string Required. The dimension name to filter.
---@field stringFilter? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaExpandedDataSetFilterStringFilter A filter for a string-type dimension that matches a particular pattern.
---@field inListFilter? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaExpandedDataSetFilterInListFilter A filter for a string dimension that matches a particular list of options.

---A logical expression of EnhancedDataSet dimension filters.
---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaExpandedDataSetFilterExpression
---@field filter? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaExpandedDataSetFilter A filter on a single dimension. This cannot be set on the top level ExpandedDataSetFilterExpression.
---@field notExpression? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaExpandedDataSetFilterExpression A filter expression to be NOT'ed (that is, inverted, complemented). It must include a dimension_filter. This cannot be set on the top level ExpandedDataSetFilterExpression.
---@field andGroup? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaExpandedDataSetFilterExpressionList A list of expressions to be AND’ed together. It must contain a ExpandedDataSetFilterExpression with either not_expression or dimension_filter. This must be set for the top level ExpandedDataSetFilterExpression.

---A list of ExpandedDataSet filter expressions.
---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaExpandedDataSetFilterExpressionList
---@field filterExpressions? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaExpandedDataSetFilterExpressionList_ A list of ExpandedDataSet filter expressions.

---@alias gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaExpandedDataSetFilterExpressionList_ gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaExpandedDataSetFilterExpression[]

---A filter for a string dimension that matches a particular list of options.
---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaExpandedDataSetFilterInListFilter
---@field values? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.StringList Required. The list of possible string values to match against. Must be non-empty.
---@field caseSensitive? boolean Optional. If true, the match is case-sensitive. If false, the match is case-insensitive. Must be true.

---A filter for a string-type dimension that matches a particular pattern.
---@class gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaExpandedDataSetFilterStringFilter
---@field value? string Required. The string value to be matched against.
---@field caseSensitive? boolean Optional. If true, the match is case-sensitive. If false, the match is case-insensitive. Must be true when match_type is EXACT. Must be false when match_type is CONTAINS.
---@field matchType? gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaExpandedDataSetFilterStringFilterMatchTypeEnum|string Required. The match type for the string filter.

---@alias gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaExpandedDataSetFilterStringFilterMatchTypeEnum "MATCH_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"EXACT"|"CONTAINS"

---@alias gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaExpandedDataSetList gcp.unstable.analyticsadmin_v1alpha.GoogleAnalyticsAdminV1alphaExpandedDataSet[]

---A link between a Google Analytics property and a Firebase project.
