---@field rowCount? number The total number of rows in the query result. `rowCount` is independent of the number of rows returned in the response, the `limit` request parameter, and the `offset` request parameter. For example if a query returns 175 rows and includes `limit` of 50 in the API request, the response will contain `rowCount` of 175 but only 50 rows. To learn more about this pagination parameter, see [Pagination](https://developers.google.com/analytics/devguides/reporting/data/v1/basics#pagination).
